# Malay names a weekday with the classifier "hari" in front of it: Kamus Dewan
# defines Isnin as "hari kedua dlm seminggu, selepas hari Ahad" and Ahad as
# "hari pertama dlm seminggu selepas hari Sabtu, hari minggu", spelling the
# classifier out every time (Kamus Dewan Edisi Keempat, Dewan Bahasa dan
# Pustaka).  Listing the classifier form as a surface is what keeps "setiap
# hari Isnin" from being read as "setiap hari" (every day) with the weekday
# discarded; bare "setiap hari" still means daily, because both readings are
# real.
isnin
hari isnin
